            },
            "text": "INTRODUCTION",
            "sentences": [],
            "annotations": [],
            "relations": []
          },
          {
            "bioctype": "BioCPassage",
            "offset": 403,
            "infons": {
              "section_type": "INTRO",
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            "text": "Currently, there is no consensus on the treatment of cystic fibrosis (CF)‐related chronic rhinosinusitis (CRS). The difference in pathophysiology between CF (neutrophilic Th1‐inflammation) and non‐CF CRS (predominantly eosinophilic Th2‐inflammation) complicates treatment validation. Increased mucus viscosity and impaired mucociliary clearance lead to bacterial colonization and biofilm formation by pathogens such as Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Staphylococcus aureus. These biofilms lead to disease recalcitrance, poor postoperative outcomes, more outpatient visits and increased antibiotic use. ",
            "sentences": [],
            "annotations": [],
            "relations": []
          },
          {
            "bioctype": "BioCPassage",
            "offset": 1009,
            "infons": {
              "section_type": "INTRO",
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            "text": "The goal of this study was to explore the in vitro efficacy of sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO3)‐enriched salts with (XNI) and without (SNI) xylitol, rhDNAse, antibiotics and bacteriophages, or combinations thereof, in reducing CF‐CRS‐related biofilms.",
            "sentences": [],
            "annotations": [],
            "relations": []
          },
          {
            "bioctype": "BioCPassage",
            "offset": 1262,
            "infons": {
              "section_type": "METHODS",
              "type": "title_1"
            },
            "text": "METHODS",
            "sentences": [],
            "annotations": [],
            "relations": []
          },
          {
            "bioctype": "BioCPassage",
            "offset": 1270,
            "infons": {
              "section_type": "METHODS",
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
            "text": "Sinonasal isolates were obtained from adult CF patients suffering from CF‐CRS during routine outpatient visits (Table 1). Ethical approval was granted by EC research UZ/KU Leuven (S64868), and informed consents were obtained.",
            "sentences": [],
            "annotations": [],
            "relations": []
          },
